WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.600
It is clear: Vladimir Putin is one of the
most controversial politicians in the world.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.750
He is idolized by some, and hated by others,
but what is for sure is that Putin’s period

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.040
in office is leaving it’s mark on international
politics.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.000
The truth is the government has achieved little
success in terms of economic and social matters

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.359
under his leadership.

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:23.570
However, his popularity among Russians remains
really high.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:32.400
Today, in this video, we’re going to analyse
why Putin is so popular in Russia.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:40.329
There is this Spanish saying that says: After
the storm, comes the calm.

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:43.050
&nbsp;
Well, when it comes to Russia, this is exactly

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.050
what has happened.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.390
&nbsp;
After going through a tough crisis in the

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.530
last few years due to the fall in the oil
prices and raw materials, as well as the sanctions

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:52.820
received from the International Community
for occupying Crimea; the government has been

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.780
pretty blunt: the difficult times have passed,
and the Russian economy is back.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.740
But… is it really?

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.390
I mean what is the evidence to show this…

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:05.700
So, what do you think growth for Russian in
2017 is expected to be?

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.140
12%? 9?

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.140
5?

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.140
3?

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.140
2???...Nope!

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.469
It´ll be 1%.

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:16.130
“Month after month, the Russian economy
keeps growing.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:21.890
For 2017 we are expecting a growth of 1%...
or even more” Igor Shuválov

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.380
Sure doesn’t look like a lot…

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.159
&nbsp;
And that is bearing in mind that Russia is

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:27.810
not exactly a rich country to begin with.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:31.601
And to be honest that one percent is only
if we believe the statistics of the Russian

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:32.601
government… which…

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:33.601
well…

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:36.259
more and more analysts are considering to
be rather fictitious.

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:37.670
&nbsp;
The truth is that, even though everything

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:42.049
seems to indicate that the Russian economy
is more stable, the last few years have not

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:44.310
exactly been easy for the Russians…

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.830
&nbsp;
According to the Russian Social Security Institute,

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:52.280
in the year 2016 alone, Russian citizens suffered
from the biggest loss in purchasing power,

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:57.189
meaning real income, since the 1990s…Not
good.

00:01:57.189 --> 00:02:02.060
The crisis and the depreciation of the rouble,
the Russian currency, has caused this country

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:07.409
with 145 million inhabitants to have a similar
GDP to the one in Australia, whose population

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.149
is only 23 million.

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:11.831
&nbsp;
And what’s even worse is that for now, it

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.500
doesn't look like the situation is going to
improve.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.980
So, here we come to the great Russian anomaly.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:21.940
Evidence which shows this country is different
to any other…

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:26.530
Neither the crisis nor the terrible economic
conditions have damaged the national popularity

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:27.530
of Vladimir Putin.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:31.980
In fact, Putin’s popularity is today almost
higher than it has ever been.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.209
According to the polls of the Levada Center,
Putin's approval among the Russian population

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:37.560
is almost 80%.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:46.830
And have a look at this:
But you might be wondering: How is this even

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:47.830
possible?

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.680
Why is this man immune to such a crisis?

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:56.070
Well, let’s have a look at what is happening…

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.790
THE PROTECTIVE FATHER

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.840
When discussing the Russian economy, it is
pretty mandatory to talk about oil and raw

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.840
materials.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.700
And here are two pieces of information so
you can get an idea of how dependent Russia

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.370
is on these two resources:
Before the fall in the prices of crude oil,

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:20.510
oil and natural gas meant a lot: 70% of the
country´s exports and more than 50% of all

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:26.250
the income of the Russian government.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:30.079
And take a look at the evolution of the price
of oil during the years Putin has been in

00:03:30.079 --> 00:03:31.090
office…

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.300
So, anyway, Putin was incredibly lucky!

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.859
Right after he reached power, the price of
oil, which had remained stable around 20$

00:03:38.859 --> 00:03:42.099
a barrel for the last 10 years, started to
increase quickly.

00:03:42.099 --> 00:03:46.120
And, of course, this meant an amazing flow
of money coming into the country.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.030
Just so you can get an idea of how significant
this was, the share the government contributed

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:54.049
to the economy rose from 35% to 70%!

00:03:54.049 --> 00:03:59.490
All of a sudden, prosperity came to the entire
nation: there were cranes everywhere, skyscrapers

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:03.480
started to appear as if they were mushrooms
after the rain, and the standard of living

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.810
for the Russians went up and up.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:11.510
Yes, it is true, Putin’s authoritarianism
could be felt from the very beginning...but,

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.510
so what?

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:13.510
Who cares!

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.930
The money was flowing!

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:21.799
We could say there was a sort of agreement
between Russian society and their leader:

00:04:21.799 --> 00:04:26.930
in exchange for not asking about civil liberties
or corruption, the government gave prosperity

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:29.020
and stability to the citizens.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:32.550
In a way Putin became some kind of protective
father to the nation.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.460
A tough but capable father, able to take care
of his children.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:40.990
But, as always, the problem is that these
situations are fragile: no government, not

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:50.090
even Putin’s, has the capacity of achieving
prosperity all on its own.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:53.830
With such high oil prices, Putin didn’t
conduct any reforms in Russia.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.710
I mean what would be the point?

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:00.240
And because of that, when the price of oil
started to go down in the summer of 2014,

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.720
the economy in Russia followed the same pattern.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:07.240
And it is here that we come to the most interesting
part....

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.310
None of these things affected Putin’s popularity.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.410
The Russian president knew, for want of a
better word, how to “recycle” his earlier

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.410
strategy.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:19.150
If at the beginning he was the guardian of
prosperity, now he would become the leader

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:26.120
who would recover the previous great influence
that mother Russia used to have!

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.229
NACIONALIST FERVOR

00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:34.250
So, if the Russia’s economy wasn’t having
its best moment, he had to look for another

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.680
source of popularity.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.400
And Putin knew where to find it…

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.620
For 500 years Russia’s foreign policy was
all about expanding it’s influence.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.660
Since the times of Ivan the Terrible, around
the 14th Century, Russia expanded its territory

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:53.550
an average of 80 sq km a day until it became,
by far, the largest country on Earth, as well

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:54.680
as the most powerful.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.629
&nbsp;
However, after the fall of the Soviet Union,

00:05:56.629 --> 00:05:59.830
the influence Russia had on the rest of the
world collapsed.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:14.250
So, Putin made a new promise, and it could
be summarized like this:

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:25.009
It may not be a prosperous country and the
economic situation may be bad, but I, Vladimir

00:06:25.009 --> 00:06:28.220
Putin, will recover Russia’s influence in
the world.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:34.210
You may not be a wealthy people, but your
nation will be strong.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:40.190
But, in order to make the strategy work, some
things are necessary:

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:45.050
The first of them is to praise nationalist
sentiment, and this means: Russia, Russia,

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:46.380
and more Russia.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:52.520
“Vladimir Putin unveils statue of medieval
namesake who 'united Russian lands' The Telegraph”

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:56.289
By the way, following these same ideals are
the recurring adverts (propaganda) of new

00:06:56.289 --> 00:07:01.280
invincible weapons, incredible powerfully
ones which will guarantee Russia gains great

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.699
status and global supremacy.

00:07:03.699 --> 00:07:08.120
First of all, an important question is going
to be whether the Russian government can actually

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.570
afford these weapons.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:14.919
The second necessary thing is rather more
sinister, and that’s for Russia to find

00:07:14.919 --> 00:07:15.919
an enemy.

00:07:15.919 --> 00:07:19.940
An enemy that can push Russians towards a
common goal....

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:24.280
&nbsp;
Let me explain: they need a threat, an aggressor,

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:27.460
a target for the Russians to unite against.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:34.870
And, to achieve that, Putin requires an aggressive
foreign policy...

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:39.330
The Ukrainian crisis, the accusations against
NATO, and the occupation of Crimea, are all

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:42.760
examples that have made Putin’s popularity
rise again.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:49.439
In the eyes of the Russians, Putin is taking
Russia back to its previous grandeur.

00:07:49.439 --> 00:07:55.949
This second strategy can explain the busy
schedule of Russian diplomacy in the last

00:07:55.949 --> 00:07:57.080
few years.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:02.370
They may not have much money, but Moscow is
everywhere, Ukraine: Syria, North Africa…

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:06.930
And hey, to be honest, the sanctions the international
community have imposed on Russia have had

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:11.770
the opposite effect that was intended: they
have been seen by the Russians as a humiliating

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:16.439
and, if they have had any effect, it was to
consolidate popular support for Vladimir Putin.

00:08:16.439 --> 00:08:23.199
“74% of the Russians consider the sanctions
to be an intention to weaken and humiliate

00:08:23.199 --> 00:08:28.939
Russia, only 5% think of them as an instrument
to stop the conflict in Ukraine” Levada

00:08:28.939 --> 00:08:29.939
Center

00:08:29.939 --> 00:08:34.620
And last of all for Putin, it is necessary
for him to consolidate the image of a strong,

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.160
determined leader.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:40.370
Almost a national hero, a savior if you will...

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.830
“There is no Russia today if there is no
Putin".

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.950
Vyacheslav Volodin, Kremlin Deputy Chief of
Staff

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:48.180
So, these are the keys in understanding why
Vladimir Putin has been able to keep and even

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.180
increase his popularity.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:54.790
He is no longer the guardian of prosperity,
but the leader who will regain the power that

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:59.490
Russia once had.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:02.430
CRONY CAPITALISM

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:06.779
Another decisive matter to be considered is
that Putin’s government also survives because

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:11.510
he has been able to create a network of powerful
oligarchs around him who have grown rich thanks

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:13.690
to the resources of the Russian state.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:17.760
Government aid, large state contracts, and
Putin’s commitment to replace imports, &nbsp;have

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:19.790
all benefited these oligarchs.

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:25.410
“Putin’s Former Judo Partner Awarded Contract
To Build Russian Bridge To Crimea.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:27.480
It'll cost more tan $3 billion”.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:28.480
&nbsp;Huffingtonpost

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:31.840
Besides, Putin has a back up plan in case
things go awry.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:37.220
He can “privatize”, or more accurately,
give state companies away to these oligarchs

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.970
who will use their power and money to further
Putin’s interests.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:43.570
&nbsp;
The Russian president has made it clear: only

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:49.610
strategic investors will be allowed to participate
in privatizations, that is investors who are

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:52.660
selected and invited by the Russian government.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:56.540
IRON FIST

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:59.270
And we can’t forget the repression.

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:03.880
Political repression and repression of minorities
seem to be the fetishes of all dictators and

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.310
potential dictators.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:10.010
Just take a look at the last report of Amnesty
International on human rights in Russia.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:15.300
It’s sad
“Restrictions on rights to freedom of expression,

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.810
association and peaceful assembly increased
in 2016.”

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:19.810
Amnesty International.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:25.760
Well, now we know the ingredients that explains
Putin’s popularity: nationalism, oligarchs,

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:28.320
censorship, and political repression.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.540
&nbsp;
Putin has promised the people to become powerful

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:34.000
again in exchange for their unconditional
loyalty.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.769
&nbsp;
However, despite the posturing, it seems unlikely

00:10:37.769 --> 00:10:42.880
for Russia to seriously be able to compete
with the US or China both in the medium and

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:44.339
the long run.

00:10:44.339 --> 00:10:48.190
But now, what do you think?

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:51.360
Will Putin succeed in giving Russia its old
power back?

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:55.950
And what would you prefer: national power,
or wellbeing, prosperity and freedom?

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:59.920
We definitely know what we’d want, but now
we want to know about you, drop us a comment

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:02.680
below this video with your thoughts.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.950
&nbsp;
